<Base title="Privacy: Crustulator" description="Crustulator has no accounts and no tracking. Your recipes stay on your device or in your browser.">
  <article>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>The short version: Crustulator has no accounts, no ads and no analytics. Your doughs stay with you.</p>
    <p>Last updated <time datetime="2026-09-15">September 15, 2026</time></p>

    <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
    <p>
      Your recipes, saved doughs, bake plans and settings are stored on your iPhone by the app or in your browser when you use the web app. They are never uploaded to us. Deleting the app or clearing the site data for crustulator.com removes them for good.
    </p>

    <h2>No tracking</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>There is no sign in and nothing to create an account for.</li>
      <li>There are no analytics, advertising or tracking tools in the app or on our websites.</li>
      <li>We do not sell, share or rent any information because we do not collect it in the first place.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Reminders</h2>
    <p>
      When you turn on bake plan reminders your phone schedules them locally. The notifications are created and delivered on your device without passing through a server.
    </p>

    <h2>Share links</h2>
    <p>
      When you share a recipe its numbers and name are packed into the link itself. Anyone who has the link can open that recipe. We do not keep a copy of shared recipes anywhere.
    </p>

    <h2>Websites and hosting</h2>
    <p>
      crustulator.app and crustulator.com are static websites. Like any web host, our hosting provider may keep standard server logs such as IP addresses and browser types for security and reliability.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes and questions</h2>
    <p>
      If anything about this ever changes we will update this page first. Questions are welcome on <a href="https://github.com/flavormingo/crustulator/issues">GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
